// The weather patterns (notes/lumina-weather-design: 8 patterns + ASH_FALL). Read by weather.Pattern.Table.
//   kind:          Pattern.Kind
//   sky:           sky.SkyModifiers at full strength (overcast, snow, haze, warmth, saturation, sunStrength)
//   fog:           colour SKY (the horizon, as the clear sky) | GREY (horizon desaturated by `desaturate`, darkened
//                  by `darken`) | WHITE | SAND (`tint` * horizon luma) | ASH (`tint` * horizon luma);
//                  density: multiplier on the climate's baseline fog density
//   precipitation: kind NONE | RAIN | SNOW | SAND | ASH, intensity [min, max] drawn per slot
//   wind:          [min, max] drawn per slot, 0 still to 1 gale
//   ground:        NONE | WET | SNOW_COVER | DUST | ASH
//   persistence:   the pattern's weight to follow itself (the diagonal of the forecast's affinity matrix);
//                  0 means it never follows itself (storms)
//   hours:         [min, max] game hours the pattern lasts from the slot's start; absent = the whole 8-hour slot
